WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.849
Energy retrofitting in buildings is a key lever to reduce GHG emissions in urban areas as 36% of energy-related emissions globally come from the building sector.

00:00:09.849 --> 00:00:13.849
In Europe, a few additional factors call our attention.

00:00:13.849 --> 00:00:18.850
One of them is that 80% of the existing buildings are projected to remain in use by 2050.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:21.850
The majority of them are old and energy-inefficient.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:29.850
Therefore, retrofitting, not new construction, is the lever to meet the GHG emission reduction target set by the EU Commission.

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.850
And in Spain, there is an additional challenge.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:39.850
Two-thirds of the population lives in multifamily buildings, which makes decisions to energy retrofitting even more complex,

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:43.850
as decisions are agreed collectively and hard to reach.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:48.850
Governments at all levels agree on the need to scale up retrofits in residential buildings,

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:56.850
and public money for energy renovations exists at EU, national and municipal level, but still uptake remains low.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:04.849
Findings of my PhD research showed that a key obstacle is that communities cannot see in one place what the works would cost,

00:01:04.849 --> 00:01:11.849
what public funds are available, and what each household will end up paying, so collective decisions stall.

00:01:11.849 --> 00:01:19.849
What RetroFin AI does is packaging the whole retrofit process, from the first estimate to the bank loan and construction works.

00:01:19.849 --> 00:01:28.849
What I also found throughout my PhD fieldwork in Madrid is that trusted community members are decisive in the neighborhood of Orcasitas,

00:01:28.849 --> 00:01:31.849
where 70% of the buildings were retrofitted.

00:01:31.849 --> 00:01:37.849
So we pair the platform with trained neighborhood champions rather than relying on software alone.

00:01:37.849 --> 00:01:44.849
RetroFin AI provides an AI-powered platform that streamlines the process of an energy retrofit in a given building.

00:01:44.849 --> 00:01:48.849
The first step is you enter your building's address on the opening page.

00:01:48.849 --> 00:01:51.849
The platform pulls the building's details straight from the cadastre.

00:01:51.849 --> 00:01:55.849
Year of construction, number of floors and units, energy performance rates.

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:59.849
The second step consists of building archetype matching.

00:01:59.849 --> 00:02:06.849
It gives the community of homeowners an initial estimate of overall cost and project timings according to the corresponding building archetype.

00:02:07.849 --> 00:02:13.849
Then, in the third step, architects confirm that estimate on site and they finalize the project proposal.

00:02:13.849 --> 00:02:18.849
This is then sent out to building companies to request quotes and compare them.

00:02:18.849 --> 00:02:24.849
On the fourth step, now with the final version of the project plan and budget,

00:02:24.849 --> 00:02:30.849
the platform integrates which funding combination, public and private, the building is actually eligible for.

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:36.849
It designs the financing plan so the community sees exactly how much they will pay and save.

00:02:36.849 --> 00:02:43.849
And finally, in step 5, the numbers are updated in the platform and the final costs, subsidies and bank loan are confirmed.

00:02:43.849 --> 00:02:46.849
Now the community is ready to vote and works can begin.

00:02:46.849 --> 00:02:55.849
In summary, RetroFin AI makes the whole retrofitting process simple enough for a community of homeowners in a multi-family building to take a collective decision

00:02:55.849 --> 00:02:59.849
and robust enough for banks to assess and co-fund it.

00:03:00.849 --> 00:03:02.849
Thank you.
